Prepare this host's context-independent controller prerequisites: the private execution bundle and the baseline native packages. Setup selects no context; the prerequisites a context adds are installed by the controller stage of apply. --dry-run previews the plan with unverified checks and makes no changes. --purge-old-bundles retires the superseded execution bundles this host still holds after the setup completes, and first, before it publishes, when a new bundle would not fit within the host's bound of 16. It first cancels a setup left pending, at that bound or below it, that never took effect and that this executable cannot resume, then sets the host up afresh. It removes no client closure and nothing the current receipt names. Review the plan before confirming; --yes skips ordinary confirmation.

Usage:
  bootwright setup [flags]

Examples:
  bootwright setup --dry-run

Flags:
      --dry-run             Limit work to the command's dry-run boundary
      --purge-old-bundles   Retire the execution bundles this host no longer needs
      --yes                 Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

Global Flags:
      --context string             Ignored: setup selects no context
  -h, --help                       Show help for this command
      --ssh-ask-sudo-password      Request the borrowed account's sudo password
      --ssh-id-file string         Offer an explicit private key for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user string            Borrow an explicit POSIX account for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user-for-provisioned   Extend the borrowed account to provisioned machines
